==Old English==

===Etymology===
From Germanic ''*akusi'', from an earlier ''*akwusi-'', possibly from Indo-European ''*ak-, *ok-'' ‘sharp, pointed’.  Cognate with Old Frisian [[axa]], Old Saxon [[akus]] (Saxon {{term|ęx|lang=nds}}), Dutch [[aaks]], Old High German [[ackus]] (German [[Axt]]), Old Norse [[øx]], [[ax]], Gothic {{Goth|[[𐌰𐌵𐌹𐌶𐌹]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/æks/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
